                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game had a lot of potential, but sadly, it is hot garbage.\n\nThe social aspect:\n1.- The game is full of cheaters that never get banned.\n2.- If you complain or report, nothing happens.\n3.- If you get mad (and eventually you will), and curse in the in-game chat at the cheaters, they report you and the idiots at Bethesda ban you for the COC or whatever these morons call it.\n\nThe game is full of blood where you kill and dismember the other players, but if you type in a bad word or are \"rude\" in chat then you are banned.  Make it make sense.\n\nTechnical issues:\nAll of the game issues, including moderation from the blue haired assholes at Bethesda, garbage server performance (rubber banding even today) and high ping, useless cheat detection, etc. are thanks to these greedy trash monetization that required centralized Bethesda only servers.  Now they gave up, and the game has no monetization (other that a purchase price) but the issues remain.  What a bunch of idiots...  The game always ran bad for what it was, due to some strange non-ID game engine.  Imagine an ID game and they pick some random garbage engine... I can go on and on... For example, the netcode handles different \"champions\" (classes) differently, so you need to learn to aim differently depending on the target.  That's why you see complete retards W+M1 all match on Eisen or Death Knight, only to end up number one in their team because nobody can hit them reliably.  Same with Galena, and the fat lizzard... It's all retarded and if you complain... The try-hard player base will tell you to learn to play, then you get more mad, curse, and then...  banned due to COC, you are bad in the chat, you are banned... Just an amazing experience! /sarcasm\n\nNo wonder there are so few players.  It's a waste of time and it's rarely fun. A shame... If the game did not have potential, it would have been better since I would have dedicated time to better games.",
